{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Like the beast, etc.</b> After they came out of the sea, HaShem led them through the wilderness. Like a beast that goes down into a valley gently, so the spirit of HaShem guided Israel." "Now <b>תניחנו</b> is in place of תניחם (you cause them to rest). The correct reading is that the vav of תניחנו reverts to Moses, and it adds: thus You led Your people — and behold, Moses and Israel."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 63, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:49.114918866Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}